--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ad496817cc2ac7b498b32f0fc2de6fb3, type: 3}
  m_Name: R1_04_BrokenCrossing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalEntry
  title: "4 \xB7 Broken Crossing"
  pages:
  - bigIdea: "Momentum is mass times velocity: p = m\xB7v. It's how much \"oomph\"
      a moving thing carries."
    notes: 'When the aqueduct collapsed, its rubble sealed the way. Pushing won''t
      move it, but a crate that hits hard enough will smash through. Not just fast,
      not just heavy: both. Each wall shows the momentum it needs.'
    lookCloser: "p = m \xD7 v   (kg\xB7m/s)\nA Burst is an impulse, and impulse =
      change in momentum: J = \u0394p\nSo every crate gets <color=#896923>15 kg\xB7m/s</color>:
      1 kg at 15 m/s, 3 kg at 5 m/s."
    funFact: A tennis ball and a bowling ball can have the same momentum. The tennis
      ball just has to be much, much faster.
    marginP1: Same Burst. Same momentum. Huh.
    marginP2: But the light one goes way faster.
    diagram:
      show: 1
      objectLabel: 'Crate

        1 kg'
      forces:
      - label: Burst
        newtons: 15
        direction: 0
        kind: 5
        unit: "N\xB7s"
      caption: "Same impulse, same momentum: 15 kg\xB7m/s for any crate."
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  - bigIdea: Friction takes momentum away every second. Heavy crates lose it faster.
    notes: "Here's the catch: the heavy crate leaves with the same 15 kg\xB7m/s,
      but friction grips it three times harder, so it's stopped before it reaches
      the rubble. The light crate keeps sliding."
    lookCloser: "Friction removes \u03BC\xB7m\xB7g of momentum every second:\n1 kg
      <color=#7d3029>9.8</color>   2 kg <color=#7d3029>19.6</color>   3 kg <color=#7d3029>29.4</color> 
      kg\xB7m/s each second\nAfter a Burst: 3 kg stops in 15 \xF7 29.4 \u2248 0.5
      s, 1 kg lasts 15 \xF7 9.8 \u2248 1.5 s."
    funFact: 'This is why a heavy truck needs good brakes: the brakes must take away
      a lot of momentum.'
    marginP1: The big one just... gave up.
    marginP2: Friction won. Use the small one.
    diagram:
      show: 1
      objectLabel: 'Crate

        3 kg'
      forces:
      - label: Friction
        newtons: 29.4
        direction: 1
        kind: 2
        unit: N
      caption: "Friction: \u221229.4 kg\xB7m/s every second for the heavy crate."
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  - bigIdea: 'Momentum adds up: push something that''s already moving and the impulses
      stack.'
    notes: "The sluice still works. Its current pushes gently but never stops, and
      a small force for a long time is an impulse too: J = F \xD7 t. Ride a Burst
      on top of the current and the crate arrives with far more."
    lookCloser: "Current <color=#267682>25 N</color> on 1 kg, friction <color=#7d3029>9.8
      N</color> \u2192 net 15.2 N\n\u2192 the crate gains 15.2 kg\xB7m/s every second
      it rides the current.\nBurst <color=#896923>15</color> + current over 3.5 m
      \u2248 18 kg\xB7m/s; Burst alone \u2248 12."
    funFact: 'Rockets work this way: a modest push, kept up for minutes, adds up
      to enormous momentum.'
    marginP1: I kick it, the water carries it.
    marginP2: Opening the sluice!
    diagram:
      show: 1
      objectLabel: 'Crate

        1 kg'
      forces:
      - label: Current
        newtons: 25
        direction: 0
        kind: 1
        unit: N
      - label: Friction
        newtons: 9.8
        direction: 1
        kind: 2
        unit: N
      caption: "Net 15.2 N: +15.2 kg\xB7m/s every second."
    sketch: {fileID: 0}
  tip: Walls only break for crates, and only for enough momentum. The heavy crate
    loses its momentum too fast; the light one keeps it. For the second wall, open
    the sluice so the current helps your Burst.
  sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a223fd49583fb204ab08b5d58242512e, type: 3}
  sketchCaption: 'Arrows: what powers what.'
